  "description": "Truvio Buying Assistant: an AI buying assistant for Dynamicweb 10 storefronts, by JustDynamics.\n\nA shopper describes what they need in plain language (\"everything to open a 20,000 gallon pool\", \"1,800 sq ft gable roof, full tear-off\", \"replacement union set for a 1 HP pump\", \"same as my last order but for 32 squares\"). The assistant searches the live catalog, sizes the job with your own rules, prices every line at that customer's prices with quantity breaks, checks stock per location and returns a cart-ready proposal with a live activity feed, the reasoning per line, and one \"Add all to cart\" button. Follow-up questions refine the same proposal. Everything the model proposes is re-priced by the platform before it reaches the cart.\n\nSET UP WITH DYNAMO (recommended)\nAfter installing and restarting, open Dynamo (the backend AI assistant) and type:\n\n    /truvio-buying-assistant-setup\n\nor simply \"Set up the buying assistant for this site\". The app ships a Dynamo skill that checks the installation, reads your catalog, drafts the business instructions and skills for your products, places the assistant on the product details page and on an \"Ask\" landing page, walks you through the one manual step (the Anthropic API key, unless Dynamo's own key can be reused) and verifies a first storefront run with you.\n\nWHAT IS IN THE BOX\n- \"Buying Assistant\" paragraph (item type Truvio_BuyingAssistant) with editor fields for copy, example prompts, mode (product page or standalone), business instructions and skills (\"## Skill: ...\" sections that say when they apply and how to size that kind of request).\n- Built-in tools that run inside the host: catalog search, product detail with specs and variants, price at quantity (price providers, customer agreements and quantity breaks apply), stock per stock location, categories, the shopper's account and cart, recent orders for reorders.\n- Optional MCP connection (Direct from the host, or Anthropic's connector) with a tool allowlist and a write guard, so the assistant can use backend tools such as documentation search.\n- Settings screen under Settings > Apps > Buying Assistant: API key, model (claude-opus-5 by default), effort, global instructions and skills, search query, MCP, limits, anonymous access, logging.\n- Swift 2 paragraph layout, JS and CSS served by the app; a status file Dynamo can read to verify the configuration and the last run.\n\nRequires Dynamicweb 10.27 or newer and a restart after installation. Uses the Anthropic API (a key is required; the Dynamo key is reused when present). Source and documentation: https://github.com/justdynamics/Truvio.Commerce.BuyingAssistant",
